<title>GERMANY: German Oct new car registrations up 6.9 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>German Oct new car registrations up 6.9 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>FLENSBURG, Germany 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>New car registrations in Germany rose by 6.9 percent in October from the same month in 1995, the Federal Motor Office said on Thursday. In the first 10 months of 1996, car registrations were up by 6.5 percent against a year earlier.</p>
<p>		     October	 Pct chg/Sept   Pct chg/Oct 95</p>
<p>    Cars	   285,918	  +4.1		   +6.9</p>
<p>    Trucks	 18,053	   +11.1		 +10.4</p>
<p>    All vehicles 320,069	  +2.9		   +8.2</p>
<p>				Jan-Oct 1996	Yr/Yr pct change</p>
<p>    Cars		    3,003,257		 +6.5</p>
<p>    Trucks		    162,815		 -7.3</p>
<p>    All vehicles	  3,469,122		 +6.7</p>
<p>The Motor Office also gave the following registration breakdown by manufacturer by German makers and Volkswagen AG foreign subsidiaries.</p>
<p>					 Oct 1996</p>
<p>    Volkswagen		     51,557</p>
<p>    Opel/GM			  45,674</p>
<p>    Ford (Germany)		 27,065</p>
<p>    Mercedes			 23,556</p>
<p>    BMW				20,303</p>
<p>    Audi			     19,400</p>
<p>    SEAT				4,162</p>
<p>    Skoda			     1,859</p>
<p>    Porsche			     593</p>
<p>					Jan-Oct 96    Market Share</p>
<p>    Volkswagen		     578,444	     19.3</p>
<p>    Opel/GM			  481,086	     16.0</p>
<p>    Ford			     297,103		9.9</p>
<p>    Mercedes			 248,522		8.3</p>
<p>    BMW				190,037		6.3</p>
<p>    Audi			     179,685		6.0</p>
<p>    SEAT				44,611		1.5</p>
<p>    Skoda			     17,705		0.6</p>
<p>    Porsche			    5,446		0.2</p>
<p>Note - Opel/GM figure includes Opel Corsa models made in Spain, the GM Pontiac van and GM trucks sold in Europe. The Ford figure includes Fords produced abroad and the Mercedes figure includes Mercedes cars built abroad.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
